e                cA-phN=qU is removed) / cA-P8 pM k$ ve / cA t3 ve (the edible                 vA\-phN=qU is recovered to feed to pigs) / cA ha ve [qq.v.]/          cA-phV=tJ  (Ndeclaus)    winnowing fan     cA bC\ ve  (OV)               make holes for the rice-seeds with a                                    dibbling-stick          /cf. thL\-p3 (N)/     cA-b@=qa-e  (N)               dance performed when the sown paddy is                                    covered over [JHT:AKS]          /cf. b@ (V) 'to cover', cA-ti=qa-e (N), cA-dB\=qa-e (N); but see            following subentry/     cA bX ve  (SV)                for rice stalks to sag under their own                                    weight          cA-bX=q1  (N)            final dance step at New Year's, imitating                                    sagging rice stalks [PL]     cA=b^-ma  (N)                 a variety of rice [PL]     cA-mK  (N)                    ricefield (either a swidden or a paddy                                    field)          /a more general term than h@ (N) or ti-mi (N) [qq.v.]/     cA-mC  (N)                    rice dust (can cause an allergic reaction)     cA=mu-cZ\  (N)                ropes made from the bark of the p%-cS                                    [q.v.] used to hang bamboo clappers to                                    scare birds away from the paddyfield          /cf. khZ\=mu-cZ\ (N)/          cA=mu-cZ\ tI qo cA=p>\-l>\ A\ ph@ tJ ve G-cZ\ yL /  The cA=mu-cZ\                                    are ropes for hanging up the clappers.     cA=mX\-ku  (N)                rice germ     cA mH cZ ve  (O + Vh + Vv)    cultivate rice for a living     cA ha ve  (OV)                winnow paddy (in a winnowing-tray)          /see picture in the front of GL/     cA-}B(=tA)  (N)               a rice-stalk; rice-straw          /SYN. chi-}B (N)/          cA-}B=qhB-tu  (N)        rice-straw      