stupidly grinning'/     cA-qQy  (N)                   nickname of a man who had a double finger                                    (in HwD-vQy [q.v.])          /cf. lA\-n%=qQy (N)/     cA-khZ-nI  (N)                [cf. khZ (Bn; Belab) 'gold' and nI (Bn)                                    'red']     cA-kh^  (N)                   name given to boy born on a moonlit night                                    or at midnight          /cf. kh^ (Bn); this is YP's real name [cf. yZ-p1=W (N)]/     cA-kh6  (N)                   [< Shan kh^n 'ascend; increase' [Cu 132];                                    cf. Si. khy!n]     cA-gX  (N)                    [cf. gX (N) 'spear']     cA=co-PY  (N)                 [last 2 sylls. prob. 'new life']          /cf. co (Clf; Belab) and PY (N; Mpfx)/     cA-cT  ~  cA=cT-nX\  (N)      ["Skinny": nickname]     cA-chu=p1  (N)                ["Fatty"; "Fatso": nickname]     cA-ch^  (N)                   [cf. ch^ (N) 'barking deer']          /this animal has been euphemistically substituted for P6 in the            cycle; cf. cA-P6 (N)/     cA-t8  (N)                    [Chin. Lh.] name given to an only son          /prob. & tI (Puniv) 'only' and tC (Num) 'one'; cf. ch%-t8 (N)/     cA-tK\  (N)                   [myth.] one of the couple created by }H-Pa                                    after the death of cA-nM-cA-p@ [q.v.];                                    "Adam"          /cf. na-tK\ (N)/     cA-tT  (N)                    [RL] [etym.?]     cA-th<  (N)                   [cf. th< (V) 'to dawn, be daybreak']     cA-thB  (N)                   [cf. thB-lA (N) 'rabbit']          /Lahu name of an urbanized Chin man who spoke fluent Lahu and was            one of the most knowledgeable guides to the hill villages of N.            Thailand; see Frontispiece photo/     cA-dA\  (N)                   [cf. dA\ (Vadj) 'good, good